    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "methods",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "Persistent means at least twelve of fifteen closes on one side and at most one cross; rotational means six to nine above with at least three crosses. Future residence uses evolving causal VWAP. Prior thirty-minute price and VWAP slopes use the frozen ATR-scaled cutpoints. Matching uses coarse shared context strata and leaves unmatched observations explicit. Fair-price errors compare frozen current references against the same future median close; ties and missing outcomes remain separate. Saved probability and difference intervals are shared-date cluster 95%, unadjusted for the three-question family; paired error is in native product points."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "All history is exploratory and outcomes had been viewed before the protocol. Landmarks and products are correlated; matching is not a causal adjustment. Primary Globex and local-anchor replications disagree, so their estimates cannot be pooled into a universal reference preference. No fill, spread, cost, execution or profitability result follows from residence or prediction accuracy."
    },
